  "basis": "Current donor-supported assistance and implementation follow-up support the work type, not marginal package availability or success rates. FHWA's 46% reduction concerns pedestrian crashes at marked crossings with medians/refuges; applying it to fatal and serious-injury people at prospective sites is an explicit unmeasured severity/site transfer.",
  "definitions": {
    "gift": "One $100,000 unrestricted gift counted in full. Allocation buys all-in support packages including shared operations. Other portfolio health is unquantified.",
    "additionality": "Funding additionality discounts existing public/foundation/fee-funded assistance. Incremental change probability already conditions on agencies, other advocates and preexisting project schedules. One distinct project per package; no second coalition attribution.",
    "implementation": "Expected changed projects times target crossings times realization measures operational crossings brought forward. Displaced health-equivalent crossings are independent of target realization and retain forgone health on failure.",
    "health": "Fatalities and serious nonfatal injuries are disjoint people outcomes, not added crash totals. Rates are prospective site archetype judgments, not extracted local crash counts. Each prevented event gets one finite tail; future survivors are not repeatedly assigned tails.",
    "timing": "Three years earlier operation after two years delay centrally; baseline catches up afterward. Annual event midpoint discounting plus finite postevent survival/disability discounting. No credit for historic ATP awards or past submissions.",
    "geography": "All modeled target and alternative health is assumed California residents and labeled US total. Bay includes SF. Target and displaced Bay/SF residence shares are independently adjustable; San Jose activity is not SF incidence. Positive regional health need not nest after subtracting differently located harms.",
    "cost": "Per changed-project real public and private costs are gift-date PV differences versus each project's own no-gift schedule, including capital timing, construction and maintenance. These unpriced priors are not full face-value grants or asserted procurement quotes. Exclude transfers and publicly paid assets from private costs. Subtract displaced alternative resources. Net public health opportunity costs are represented only by specific lost alternative health; no monetized health subtraction.",
    "uncertainty": "Central and favorable are uncalibrated joint assumptions, not confidence limits. No probabilities assigned to scenarios. Threshold crossing in favorable case is not evidence of high expected value.",
    "harm": "Separate donor harm is already net gift-attributable health at gift date and survives zero staff additionality. Unquantified walking activity, climate, police/community programs and other portfolio benefits are not assigned zero truth."
  },
